  "backend_parity": [
    {
      "id": "architecture_and_system_info",
      "status": "partial",
      "summary": "A UI-neutral nonblocking native worker owns the canonical architecture, Windows version, machine-name, and elevation contracts shared with Tauri. Reactor now starts that worker off the UI thread, renders the live host/OS/elevation result, exposes native/emulated architecture in the machine-card automation name, rejects stale completions, and blocks scan selection until elevation is known. A fixture-free native ARM64 run matched the Store 2.5.8 Diagnostics viewport at 1440x1000 logical / 2160x1500 physical, loaded local XAML, loaded no WebView module, closed gracefully, and produced no crash event. Elevated, error, emulated, x64, and full accessibility matrices remain open.",
